Falsifies `allocation_cache::verification::a_request_lands_in_a_class_that_holds_it`.

The defect: `class_bytes` answers one byte short of the class's grid step, so a block of the
largest request in each class is smaller than the request.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that `class_bytes(c) >= size`; Kani reports the assertion
reachable at `size = 16`.

diff --git a/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs b/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
index d42a4df59..eced71611 100644
--- a/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ pub const fn class(size: usize, align: usize) -> Option<usize> {
 
 /// The effective size of a class's blocks.
 pub const fn class_bytes(class: usize) -> usize {
-    (class + 1) * GRID
+    (class + 1) * GRID - 1
 }
 
 /// The layout every block of `class` is allocated from, and freed to, the heap under.
